  "body": "A number of callers don't give it and callers do check for parent being non-null before calling. It seems we should assert it's non-null and then use that. I.e., turn the internal concept into being closer to `child.remove()` rather than `parent.removeChild(child)`.\r\n\r\nBonus: clean up attribute removal in a similar fashion.",
